  "description": "Local-first .NET global tool that checks a stack/config contract before runtime.\n\nstackcontract validates Docker Compose and/or appsettings against a stackcontract.yml contract, then reports missing services, env keys, and configuration paths. It does not start containers and does not need a Docker daemon for `validate`. Local .env and appsettings are inspected for key/path presence only — values never appear in text or JSON output. Compose is optional for plain C# / ASP.NET apps.\n\nCommands: `stackcontract init` writes a contract from compose and/or appsettings (and optional Options assemblies); `stackcontract validate [--strict] [--environment NAME]` checks the live tree; `stackcontract version` prints the tool version. Exit codes: 0 ok/warnings, 1 any error, 2 usage/parse. Finding codes include SVC_MISSING, ENV_*, CONFIG_PATH_MISSING, CONFIG_PARSE, COMPOSE_PARSE, CONTRACT_INVALID, PROFILE_UNKNOWN.\n\nLegacy ComposeContract names still work: composecontract.yml is accepted when stackcontract.yml is absent. MIT licensed. Not affiliated with Docker, Inc.\n\nInstall: `dotnet tool install -g stackcontract`. Pair with StackContract.AspNetCore to fail host start when required configuration keys are missing.",
